    {
      "text": "You can configure the scan rule to scan GitHub resources and repositories after onboarding the GitHub repositories. To learn more, see Onboarding GitHub Tenant."
    },
    {
      "text": "To configure a scan rule for GitHub repositories, complete the following steps in the AI Security Admin Portal:"
    },
    {
      "item": "1. Provide the general information.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Go to Administration > Scan Settings.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          20
        ],
        [
          23,
          36
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Select the Scan Rules tab.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          11,
          21
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Add Scan Rule.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 3,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          19
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "The General Information page appears.",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          4,
          23
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "On the General Information page:",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 4,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          26
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Scan Rule Name: Enter a unique and descriptive name for the scan rule.",
      "depth": 2,
      "number": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          14
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Scan Rule Description (Optional): Enter a description for the scan rule (maximum is 500 characters).",
      "depth": 2,
      "number": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          32
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Next.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 5,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          10
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "2. Select the cloud and resource type.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "On the Select Cloud and Resource Type page:",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          37
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "For Cloud Type, select SaaS.",
      "depth": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          4,
          14
        ],
        [
          23,
          27
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "For Service Type, select GitHub.",
      "depth": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          4,
          16
        ],
        [
          25,
          31
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Next.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          10
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "3. Select the repositories that must be scanned.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "On the Select Repositories page, select the repositories from GitHub that you want to include in the scan rule.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          26
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Next.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          10
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "4. Exclude repositories",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "On the Exclusions page, you can specify the paths in the repositories that must be excluded from the scan.",
      "depth": 0,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          17
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Define the path exclusion rules per repository.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Select the repositories you would like to set an exclusion for the scan rule.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Set rules: To set the rules, do the following:",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 2
    },
    {
      "item": "Path field: Enter the file path or pattern you want to exclude. For example, src//*.ts excludes all TypeScript files inside the src folder and its subfolders.",
      "depth": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          10
        ],
        [
          81,
          158
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Regex toggle (</> Regex): Switch to Regex mode if you need more advanced pattern matching instead of glob patterns.",
      "depth": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          25
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Add to add the entered path rule to the exclusion list.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 3,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          9
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Next.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 4,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          10
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "5. Select the scan type.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "On the Scan Type page, choose how scans are triggered and what type of scan to run.",
      "depth": 0,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          16
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Select Scheduled Full Scan to run a complete scan of all files across every selected repository on a recurring schedule is performed.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          26
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "If you do not select this option, recurring scans are not scheduled for the selected repositories, and you are taken directly to the Review page.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Next.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          10
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "6. Select the scan schedule.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "On the Scan Schedule page, choose one of the following options:",
      "depth": 0,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          20
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Daily: To scan the data every day.",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          6
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Weekly: To scan the data every week.",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          7
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Monthly: To scan the data once a month.",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          8
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "On Demand: To scan the data on demand.",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          10
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "7. Review and complete the configuration.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Review the scan rule. Click the Edit icon to change any values, if required.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          32,
          36
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Finish.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          12
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The scan rule must be enabled on the Overview page to initiate the scan."
    }
  ]
}
